      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path:</strong> A near-term ≥5-fatality Israeli airstrike cluster in Lebanon (F1 at 60%) combined with Bessent's D-Day sanctions naming Chinese entities (F6 at 28%) drives regional widening; F1 alone dominates the 45% weight.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> Talks stay frozen (F3 at 20% for a formal session) and Hormuz stays at ~10/day (F4 at 15% for 40/day recovery), yielding an attrition equilibrium anchored by Netanyahu's coalition surviving to Oct 27 (F5 at 35% for early collapse).</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> The narrow path runs through an Iran-Oman route agreement (F2 at 35%) unlocking permitted transits and creating a mediator opening; without it the 15% weight is thin.</p>
